For part (i), we need to show that Marco might need to reserve at least n different tables.

Let me start by understanding the problem better. Each friend has some collection of stickers. A pair of friends is wholesome if together they have all n stickers. Marco wants to seat his friends at tables such that no wholesome pair is at the same table. So, each table can have any number of friends, but no two friends at the same table can form a wholesome pair.

So, the problem is equivalent to coloring the friends with colors (tables) such that no two friends who form a wholesome pair have the same color. This is similar to a graph coloring problem, where each friend is a vertex, and there is an edge between two friends if they form a wholesome pair. Then, the problem becomes finding the chromatic number of this graph, which is the minimum number of colors needed to color the vertices so that no two adjacent vertices have the same color.

